# Documentation

Every feature ships with code comments **and** a `Docs/` page.

## Code

- `///` on public classes, endpoints, ViewModels, repositories, and non-obvious methods
- Explain *why* (permissions, building scope, order status rules), not what the identifier already says
- Do not comment generated code

## Docs folder

Path: repo-root `Docs/` (not inside a single app).

- `Docs/README.md` — index
- `Docs/architecture.md` — layers and apps
- `Docs/features/<feature>.md` — how the feature works (actors, flows, permissions, data)

Update the feature doc in the same change as the implementation. If the user changes product direction, update Docs first or in the same PR.
